## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and no-loosening (C1).** A path beyond the one, or a byte of `DEPLOY.md`, `support.ts`, a product/config/package/lock file = **Blocker**; a fifth commit or a moved head = STOP; a person's name, real customer name or secret in an added line or message = **Blocker**; a decision-card slug = **Blocker**; an assertion removed or loosened, or an expected value of an existing row changed = **Major, class**; a work number or shape id in an added title, comment or the commit title = **Minor**.
- **G-2 kill-lost (C2, C3).** A closed case (B736-1, item (c), B707-1) no longer flagged = **Major, class**; a kill `eddebf34` or `99585f7d` flagged that `abd07d35` loses, NOT one of the 16 and not covered by a ruling proved by counterfactual = **Major, class**; the new scanner reds the real `DEPLOY.md` = **Major, class**; **one of the 16 not reproduced** = instrument not proven, C3 NOT TESTED for that cell (print both cells; never close it silently); a fresh-seed cell outside the 16 that the cross-line counterfactual proves an INSTANCE OF THE TICKETED CLASS = **outside the commission's "only 16" property: a Major of the commission, written as such, with the cell, the carrier line and the counterfactual, and it goes to the product owner's card as "same class, more instances"** (Tuesday decides the grade in Q-1; the kit's default is that it is a Major, because the commission writes "any cell outside the 16 is a FAIL"); a fresh cell NOT of that class = **Major, class (b)**; a shape a ruling (a)/(b) plausibly covers but the counterfactual cannot settle = **RULING-BOUNDARY Note**; old flags, new does not, no pty failure = **Note**; new flags, no bash failure = **Note** (except the real `DEPLOY.md`).
- **G-3 closure (C4, C6).** A named row red under no swap = **Major, class**; a swap that turns more or fewer rows red than the builder claimed = **Minor** (name them) unless a named row is lost, then Major; an original row red under a swap = a finding at the severity of its cause; a comment that claims a shell fact the pty does not show = **Major**; a builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 stability and names (C4).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; file other than 55 of 55 or group other than 514 without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 7 = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on `eddebf34` = **Major**.
- **G-5 CI, CodeQL, merge (C5, C6).** CodeQL at the head: all three check-runs `completed` `success`, both analyses present with 0 results, 0 open alerts on the PR ref and the merge ref = met. **Not met (a required check not `completed` `success`, or an analysis missing) = `CI pending: <names>`, a CONDITION on every verdict, never clean and never a code failure; landing waits for a real scan through the ruleset, never bypassed.** An open alert on the head or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with #95, #91, #86, #85 or another live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact.
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table.** Any Major or Blocker of the class (G-1 loosening, G-2, G-3) = `NO GO`; this is the product owner's short check, not a builder round: a NO GO goes to the product owner as a card with your cells attached, and FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list with cells, the RESIDUE as ticket text, and whether the closed instances can ship alone. If C2 passes and C3 Set A equals the 16 and Set B is "equals the 16 (or a subset)" or empty: `GO` (or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` for Notes and Minors). If Set B finds only class instances outside the 16: the verdict is `NO GO` by the commission's wording unless Tuesday's Q-1 answer in the Stamp says otherwise (the default, written first); say in FOR TUESDAY that the closed cases hold and what the card should ask. Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read 5.3 to 6.4 at the draft; `heavy.sh` waits). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, any vitest over more than one file, the group run, the pty containers in a batch. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the C2 harness, the clone, C5 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b755/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b755/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b755/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b755-node:head` once: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b755-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`); record node, npm, vitest versions (RELAYED: v22.23.2, 10.9.8, 5.0.0). One image serves main, `eddebf34` and the head (the trees differ in one test file). Remove ONLY your own `pc-b755-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site.** Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create. Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, merge-tree only inside `.tools/b755/repo` and `.tools/wt-b755-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders; this kit runs no unit chain. No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b755/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, no decision-card id, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane and the gate lineage and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** if your session ends at the account's weekly limit, that is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your own STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and the checks, release or reclaim any lock you held by your own rule, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names.

## PARTITION (named from both sides)
- **Yours:** the plain clone `.tools/b755/repo` and worktrees `.tools/wt-b755-{main,base,head,mut,probe}` (`-main`: main's file; `-base`: `eddebf34`'s tree for the baseline; `-head`: `abd07d35`; `-mut`: the revert, swap and corpus copies only; `-probe`: scratch), project root (untracked): your Step-0 brief copy, `Briefs/2026-10-26_B755_STATUS.md`, `Briefs/2026-10-26_B755_evidence/runs/` (never a folder named `logs`: the root `.gitignore` ignores it), `.tools/b755/`, images and containers `pc-b755-*`, ports 9460-9469 (a reserve: you publish none). B-number B755. Pane `Datasec/Security-Composer-G154`. Suffix `G154`. Findings `B755-n`.
